Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: base move b10680/d7bd3bfca -> b10819/6a1a922d2,
 and the governed sha re-key that follows it

UPDATE-RUNBOOK 2.2 manual path plus 2.2.1. arifi/main was LINEARIZED first (14 merge
commits removed; `git diff 95c1b6e69 <flattened>` EMPTY, 0 merges, 534 -> 532 commits after
two duplicate patches collapsed), because `series regen` and the merges==0 gate are
unreachable while merges exist.

Re-keyed by exact-subject match, one unique hit asserted per row, old keys appended and
never overwritten: 338 pointers across native-grandfather.json (287 rows),
protected-wins.json (21 entries) and protected-win-baseline.json. `protected-win validate`
is back to PASS with all 39 protected paths and all 41 anchors resolving in source.

Two grandfather rows dropped because their commits replayed EMPTY (already applied):
resolved/0009-vulkan-add-mul_mat_vec_id-for-the-TurboQuant-w and
resolved/0019-vulkan-dispatch-the-TQ-rotated-mul_mm_id-path.

Four escha commits were added to the baseline with written dispositions. They were always
in base..arifi/main but the discovery scan could not see them behind the merges; the
flatten exposed them, and all four are ancestors of tip_when_recorded. The ROCmFP4 MMVQ
entry was re-pointed to the head of its own mechanism (the opt-in commit), which the
entry's mechanism text already described. No field was invented.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - tooling and governed records only; no engine behaviour changed by this commit.
